# Ownership follows a capability across code, tests, documentation, and
# operations (Ownership Map, R37). This repo has one real maintainer today
# (@georgekarounias), so every path below resolves to the same owner — the
# file exists anyway to make the intended vertical seams legible on every
# PR (matching "Owning bounded context/capability" in
# .github/pull_request_template.md), and to be ready to extend the moment
# a second contributor joins.
#
# CODEOWNERS applies the LAST matching pattern, so broader/foundational
# rules are listed first and more specific overrides after — in particular,
# /clinical-knowledge/ (Clinical Knowledge) must precede /clinical-knowledge/tests/ and the AI migrations
# path below, or its broad match would win over the narrower ones.
#
# Lines marked "dual-review" are cross-context contracts or migrations
# (see R37's Validation column: "ensure cross-context contracts and
# migrations require dual review"). One real owner can't enforce that
# today — listed here so it's stated plainly, not silently absent.

# ---- Clinical Knowledge (Clinical Knowledge Team) ----
# Ingestion, document lifecycle, retrieval, grounded answers, summaries, clinical DB and adapters.
# (Ownership Map's own "Primary folders" cell for this area reads literally "clinical-knowledge/..." in the
# source workbook — an incomplete entry there; treated here as the whole clinical-knowledge/ deployable, with
# the two narrower overrides below for the parts other teams own.)
/clinical-knowledge/                                                                @georgekarounias

# ---- Runtime & Data (Platform + Data Steward) ----
# Composition, databases, migrations, observability, releases, VM/secret/runtime policy.
/ops/                                                               @georgekarounias
